{
  "about": "Golden vectors for the keyed GEX book v2 (itmatrixhq.ws.v1 GexStrikeBook = Frame field 23, GexStrikeBookUpdate = Frame field 24). Apply the steps in order to one client state. Each frame_hex is one complete Frame as one WebSocket binary message. 'state' is the client state after the step; for expect=resync the frame must be rejected (CRC of the book after applying is crc_after_applying, the frame carries a different crc), the state stays as it was, and the client sends {op:\"resync\"}. The backend asserts its own encoder reproduces every apply step byte for byte (crates/itm-api/src/stream/keyed_gex.rs, crates/itm-wire-proto/tests/gex_book_vectors.rs). SDKs copy this file verbatim.",
  "conventions": {
    "strikes": "integer thousandths of a dollar; the frame carries [0] absolute and [i>0] the delta to the previous strike (sint64)",
    "call_gex_put_gex": "float32 per-$1-move dollars, calls >= 0, puts <= 0; every value here is exactly representable",
    "gex": "derived, not sent: float64(call) + float64(put)",
    "book_id": "fixed64, given as a decimal string because it exceeds 2^53",
    "flip_point": "null when the frame does not carry it",
    "crc": "CRC-32/IEEE (zlib.crc32) over the strikes in ascending order, each as strike thousandths int64 LE, then call float32 bits LE, then put float32 bits LE",
    "update_rule": "an update applies only to the same book_id at version = state.version + 1, and only when the CRC of the book after applying equals the frame's crc",
    "engine": "update steps also give the engine grid the server diffed (relative deadband 1e-3 of the published book's largest max(|call|,|put|), both sides sent for each listed index)"
  },
